DTSTAMP:20260603T155407Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260601
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SUMMARY:Mackerel — peak season
DESCRIPTION:Summer fish\, landed at Kilkeel and the wider Down coast. Best 
 the day it comes in — flash on a hot pan\, eat with bread and butter and a
  squeeze of lemon.\n\nCategory: seafood\n\nFull guide at ulster.food
LOCATION:Ulster
URL:https://ulster.food/#season
CATEGORIES:Seafood
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:produce-7@ulster.food
DTSTAMP:20260603T155407Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260501
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SUMMARY:Lobster — peak season
DESCRIPTION:Down coast lobster from the Kilkeel and Portavogie fleets. Swee
 t\, dense flesh — the absolute peak of Irish summer eating. Boil briefly\,
  butter generously.\n\nCategory: seafood\n\nFull guide at ulster.food
LOCATION:Ulster
URL:https://ulster.food/#season
CATEGORIES:Seafood
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
