DTSTAMP:20260603T155407Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260801
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261101
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SUMMARY:Lough Neagh pollan — peak season
DESCRIPTION:Endemic to Lough Neagh — a glacial relict species found in only
  a handful of Irish loughs. Eaten on the lough shore\, exported to Switzer
 land\, almost invisible elsewhere.\n\nCategory: seafood\n\nFull guide at u
 lster.food
LOCATION:Ulster
URL:https://ulster.food/#season
CATEGORIES:Seafood
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:produce-12@ulster.food
DTSTAMP:20260603T155407Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261201
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SUMMARY:Lough Neagh eels — peak season
DESCRIPTION:PGI-protected\, caught by the Lough Neagh Fishermen's Co-operat
 ive at Toomebridge. Most are exported to Holland to be smoked. The Sargass
 o Sea to the lough and back — the great migration story of Ulster food.\n\
 nCategory: seafood\n\nFull guide at ulster.food
LOCATION:Ulster
URL:https://ulster.food/#season
CATEGORIES:Seafood
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
