DTSTAMP:20260603T155407Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260601
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260901
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SUMMARY:🌿 Samphire — peak season
DESCRIPTION:Salt-tolerant marsh samphire on the muddy shores of Strangford 
 Lough and the Down coast. Cut with scissors above the woody base. Blanch b
 riefly\, butter generously\, eat with anything from the sea.\n\nCategory: 
 veg\nWild / foraged — please forage responsibly.\n\nFull guide at ulster.f
 ood
LOCATION:Ulster
URL:https://ulster.food/#season
CATEGORIES:Veg\,Foraged
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:produce-18@ulster.food
DTSTAMP:20260603T155407Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260401
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260801
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SUMMARY:🌿 Sea spinach — peak season
DESCRIPTION:Wild sea beet on the upper shore — leafier and more interesting
  than its cultivated cousin. Look for it on the strandlines from Killyleag
 h round to Ballyhalbert. Wilts down to nothing\, so pick a proper bag.\n\n
 Category: veg\nWild / foraged — please forage responsibly.\n\nFull guide a
 t ulster.food
LOCATION:Ulster
URL:https://ulster.food/#season
CATEGORIES:Veg\,Foraged
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:produce-19@ulster.food
DTSTAMP:20260603T155407Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260801
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SUMMARY:🌿 Wild blackberries — peak season
DESCRIPTION:The August hedgerow gift. Every back lane in County Down delive
 rs them — best the day after a warm spell\, picked low to avoid the dog wa
 lkers. Fold into apple crumbles\, make jam\, freeze flat on a tray for win
 ter.\n\nCategory: fruit\nWild / foraged — please forage responsibly.\n\nFu
 ll guide at ulster.food
LOCATION:Ulster
URL:https://ulster.food/#season
CATEGORIES:Fruit\,Foraged
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:produce-20@ulster.food
DTSTAMP:20260603T155407Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261101
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SUMMARY:🌿 Chanterelles — peak season
DESCRIPTION:Golden chanterelles under the spruce in the Mournes and Tollymo
 re in late summer. Apricot-scented\, peppery\, the finest wild mushroom th
 at grows in Ulster. Only forage what you can identify with certainty.\n\nC
 ategory: mushroom\nWild / foraged — please forage responsibly.\n\nFull gui
 de at ulster.food
LOCATION:Ulster
URL:https://ulster.food/#season
CATEGORIES:Mushroom\,Foraged
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:produce-21@ulster.food
DTSTAMP:20260603T155407Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261001
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261201
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SUMMARY:🌿 Sloes — peak season
DESCRIPTION:Blackthorn fruits along the lanes\, ready after the first frost
 . Tart and astringent raw — they exist to be steeped in gin with sugar and
  patience. Pick October\, drink by Christmas.\n\nCategory: fruit\nWild / f
 oraged — please forage responsibly.\n\nFull guide at ulster.food
LOCATION:Ulster
URL:https://ulster.food/#season
CATEGORIES:Fruit\,Foraged
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
