BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:festival-6@ulster.food
DTSTAMP:20260603T155407Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260801
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260901
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SUMMARY:🎪 Ould Lammas Fair
DESCRIPTION:Nearly 400 years old — the oldest fair in Ireland. Famous for d
 ulse (the dried Atlantic seaweed eaten as a snack across Ulster) and yello
 wman (the bright honeycomb toffee). Traditional horse trading\, market sta
 lls\, street entertainment and live music fill the town for two full days.
 \n\nDates: Last Monday & Tuesday of August (~31 Aug – 1 Sep 2026)\nFocus: 
 Dulse\, yellowman\, traditional horse trading\nMore info: https://www.visi
 tcausewaycoastandglens.com/whats-on/ould-lammas-fair\n\nFull guide at ulst
 er.food
LOCATION:Ballycastle\, County Antrim
URL:https://www.visitcausewaycoastandglens.com/whats-on/ould-lammas-fair
CATEGORIES:Festival\,Heritage
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:festival-7@ulster.food
DTSTAMP:20260603T155407Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260801
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260901
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SUMMARY:🎪 Fermanagh Taste Experience
DESCRIPTION:A weekend showcase of Fermanagh's distinctive food culture — pa
 sture-fed beef\, freshwater lake fish\, farmhouse cheeses and the county's
  growing distilling scene. The lake country's answer to a food festival.\n
 \nDates: Late August\nFocus: Beef\, lake fish\, cheese\, distillery\nMore 
 info: https://www.fermanaghlakelands.com/\n\nFull guide at ulster.food
LOCATION:Enniskillen\, County Fermanagh
URL:https://www.fermanaghlakelands.com/
CATEGORIES:Festival\,Food
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
