BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:festival-11@ulster.food
DTSTAMP:20260603T155407Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SUMMARY:🎪 Hans Sloane Chocolate & Fine Food Festival
DESCRIPTION:Named for Sir Hans Sloane\, born in Killyleagh in 1660 — the ma
 n who tasted chocolate-with-milk in Jamaica and brought the idea back to E
 urope\, the seed of what later became Cadbury's. The festival is held at K
 illyleagh Castle\, sponsored by Finnebrogue Artisan\, with chocolatiers fr
 om across the UK and Ireland alongside the finest NI artisan food producer
 s.\n\nDates: September (biennial)\nFocus: Chocolate\, NI artisan fine food
 \nMore info: http://www.hanssloane.com/\n\nFull guide at ulster.food
LOCATION:Killyleagh Castle\, Killyleagh
URL:http://www.hanssloane.com/
CATEGORIES:Festival\,Food
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:festival-12@ulster.food
DTSTAMP:20260603T155407Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SUMMARY:🎪 Portaferry Heritage Fest
DESCRIPTION:30+ events across three days celebrating the peninsula's histor
 y\, landscape and food culture. The standout for Ulster.food is the Wild A
 bout Foraging event at Kearney — forage\, cook and eat with wildlife exper
 t David Thompson and wild chef Celia Spouncer on the Strangford Lough shor
 e. A direct introduction to the foraging story.\n\nDates: 13–15 September\
 nFocus: Heritage\, foraging\, peninsula food culture\nMore info: https://s
 trangfordlough.org/news/launch-of-portaferry-heritage-fest/\n\nFull guide 
 at ulster.food
LOCATION:Portaferry\, Ards Peninsula
URL:https://strangfordlough.org/news/launch-of-portaferry-heritage-fest/
CATEGORIES:Festival\,Heritage
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:festival-13@ulster.food
DTSTAMP:20260603T155407Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261001
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261101
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SUMMARY:🎪 Strangford Lough Oyster Festival
DESCRIPTION:The oyster festival on the lough itself — smaller and more root
 ed than Hillsborough. Stalls and shucking displays along the Strangford wa
 terfront\, plus workshops on sustainable oyster farming and marine ecology
 . Oysters served come from certified local farms using sustainable methods
